ses animal models, cell culture, molecular and histological approaches, and transcriptomic analyses to better understand mec... View Details Bookmark Network Engineer I S07209P Information Technology-Enterprise Tech. Innovation & Serv Staff 09/02/2026 The Network Engineer I is an entry-level professional position responsible for supporting the operation, maintenance, and monitoring of the University of Texas at Dallas enterprise network infrastructure. This role works under the guidance of senior network engineers and management to ensure reliable, secure, and high-performing wired and wireless network services that support the academic, res... View Details Bookmark Child Development Specialist III - Preschool S07083P Callier Ctr Communication Staff 06/05/2026 Looking for a rewarding opportunity to work with children? Join our Callier Center Team!The Callier Center provides a nurturing, learning environment for infants through kindergarten Age. We focus on developing every child’s specific needs, including communication and language skills, physical abilities, emotional and social growth and cognitive development. Our Program fosters an environment i... View Details Bookmark Program Manager, Davidson Management Honors Program (JSOM) S07213P Management Staff 08/31/2026 The Program Manager serves as a key member of the Davidson Management Honors Program (DMHP) and is responsible for the planning, coordination, implementation, and assessment of programs and services that support student success, leadership development, engagement, recruitment, and community building. Reporting to the DMHP Director and working closely with the DMHP Associate Dean, this position ... View Details Bookmark Tax Accountant S07088P Payroll Staff 08/31/2026 The Tax Accountant reports to the Tax Compliance Manager and is responsible for the analysis, record keeping, payments, and reporting functions related to federal and state tax compliance. Responsibilities also include pension fund reconciliation and reporting, the completion of an annual UBIT analysis and private use survey, and communicating with tax authorities and individuals. Performs reco... View Details Bookmark LARC Technician S07212P Research Operations & Labs Staff 08/31/2026 To assist in the maintenance and operation of the animal experimentation/research facilities. Responsible for the performance of routine non-technical tasks.The training schedule for the Animal Technician is M-F, 8am-5pm. Once adequate training is accomplished (a few weeks depending on experience) new technicians are required to work the weekends and take 2 days off during the week. View Details Bookmark Postdoctoral Research Associate S07208P Neuroscience Staff 08/28/2026 The Department of Neuroscience and the Center for Advanced Pain Studies at UT Dallas has an opening for a postdoctoral research associate to join the Price Lab.This specific position will work on NIH grant funded projects that are aimed at better understanding how neuronal plasticity alters the way the brain receives nociceptive information from the sensory system and how this relates to chroni... View Details Bookmark Open-Rank Non-Tenure System Faculty position - Clinical Professor/Professor of Practice and Program Director F01169P Executive Education Faculty 09/30/2026 08/28/2026 Position Description The Naveen Jindal School of Management is seeking a non-tenure track Clinical Professor/Professor of Practice and Program Director to lead the Alliance for Physician Leadership (APL) program, a nationally recognized Healthcare Leadership & Management Executive MS/MBA exclusively for physician leaders.  The program’s over 750 physician graduates currently occupy senior h... View Details Bookmark Food Service Worker II S07193P Callier Ctr Communication Staff 08/28/2026 The Food Service Worker II at the Callier Child Development Center plays a vital role in supporting daily kitchen operations by assisting with food preparation, maintaining accurate records, and upholding high standards of quality and safety.This position offers opportunities for growth through cross‑training in all areas of food service. The ideal candidate delivers excellent customer service,... View Details Bookmark Financial Services Assistant S07210P Computer Science Staff 09/07/2026 08/27/2026 Works closely with department faculty and staff to provide financial and research management and administration for the department finances, financial processes, and records to meet the department’s day-to-day financial operations goals. Assist in ensuring compliance with all regulations, policies, and university requirements are met to secure the department’s long-term financial viability and ... View Details Bookmark Assistant Director for Facilities Services S07111P Facilities Management Staff 06/25/2026 Responsible for the management of the Main Campus facilities services operations and programs (Custodial, Grounds, Garage, Signs & Keys, Move & Events, and Maintenance & Construction). Shares responsibility with another Assistant Director for the management of department operations in the absence of the Director of Facilities Services & Operations. View Details Bookmark Part-time Lecturer - Mechanical Engineering F01168P Mechanical Engineering Faculty 07/31/2027 08/18/2026 Lecturers teach one or more undergraduate and/or graduate sections in a given term. Appointments carry no guarantee or expectation of renewal or tenure. View Details Bookmark Program Specialist II S07207P Interdisciplinary Studies Staff 09/30/2026 08/25/2026 The position is responsible for providing expertise to implement, develop, and evaluate enrollment initiatives, develop recruitment strategies, and assist the department of Interdisciplinary Studies with strategic implementation of recruitment activities by identifying strong recruitment approaches and developing outreach programs. View Details Bookmark Finance Operations Coordinator S07206P Electrical and Computer Engineering Staff 08/25/2026 Looking for a rewarding career opportunity with great benefits? Interested in joining a dynamic & fun group of professionals? Look no further! Join our team! The University of Texas at Dallas has an excellent job opportunity for individuals looking to join the Erik Jonsson School of Engineering and Computer Science as a Finance Operations Coordinator. This position will provide budgeting, f... View Details Bookmark Associate Director - JSOM Career Management Center (CMC) S07205P Management Staff 08/23/2026 The Associate Director in the Jindal School of Management (JSOM) Career Management Center (CMC) is a strategic leader dedicated to advancing the career success of Undergraduate students. This role focuses exclusively on the undergraduate audience, designing and executing meaningful networking, internship, and career opportunities with employers actively seeking top talent. The position operates... View Details Bookmark Academic Advisor II S07201P NSM Deans Office Staff 08/21/2026 Academic advisors provide specialized academic advising services to students and advising-based perspectives to University colleagues and public stakeholders, such as students, family-members and prospective students. By integrating excellent interpersonal and communication skills with knowledge or curricula, policies (departmental, School, and University), resources, and student development, t... View Details Bookmark Postdoctoral Research Associate S07123P Texas Medical Device Center Staff 07/01/2026 The Postdoctoral Research Associate will work as a research fellow within the Larynx Lab at the Texas Biomedical Device Center, supporting active projects in recovery from neurological injuries, vagus nerve stimulation, laryngeal dysfunction, and implantable neural devices, as well as developing their own ideas for new projects. Efforts will focus on working with pre-clinical models which facil... View Details Bookmark Media Technology Specialist II S07198P Educational Technology Services Staff 08/17/2026 This position supports the preparation, setup, operation, maintenance, troubleshooting, and continued advancement of the university’s immersive projection classroom and its Pixera-based visualization environment. Working closely with the lead technician assigned to the immersive classroom, this position assists with classroom operations, preventative maintenance, technical support, and instruct... View Details Bookmark Media Technology Specialist III S07199P Educational Technology Services Staff 08/17/2026 This position serves as the lead technician for the university’s immersive projection classroom and is responsible for the preparation, setup, operation, maintenance, troubleshooting, and continued advancement of its Pixera-based visualization environment and associated audiovisual systems.The position will diagnose and resolve complex technical issues, perform preventative maintenance, and ens... View Details Bookmark Payroll Specialist I S07197P Payroll Staff 08/14/2026 Under the general direction of the Payroll Manager, the Payroll Specialist I provides technical skills required in the processing of payrolls and related data within a highly technical payroll system. Responsible for preparing and submitting payrolls and related monthly reports.The Payroll Specialist I is responsible for ensuring that all time and labor setup is complete for new and existing em... View Details Bookmark Research Clinician S07196P BrainHealth Project Staff 08/14/2026 The Clinician role is responsible for delivering brain health assessments, coaching, and training services through the Center for BrainHealth. This role administers and interprets the Concierge BrainHealth Index, prepares reports, provides client feedback, and maintains ongoing client relationships. The position collaborates with an interdisciplinary team to develop individualized performance r... View Details Bookmark Media Technology Specialist I S07189P Educational Technology Services Staff 08/14/2026 Under direct to general supervision, provides faculty, staff and students with technical support in the operation and set-up of media equipment. Provide professional and courteous instruction to faculty and staff in the proper use and handling of AV equipment. Will assist in maintaining a schedule of preventative maintenance. Must be dependable, reliable and be able to work both independently a... View Details Bookmark Lab Manager S07191P Neuroscience Staff 08/12/2026 The Price Lab is seeking to hire a Laboratory Manager to be responsible for overseeing and supervising laboratory personnel, ensuring adherence to safety protocols, managing lab resources, and overseeing daily operations. This role requires strong leadership, organizational skills, and technical expertise to maintain high-quality standards in laboratory practices.The Price Laboratory, at UT Dal... View Details Bookmark Administrative Coordinator S07181P CBH-Walker Staff 08/07/2026 The Administrative Coordinator provides high-level, complex, and confidential administrative support to the Director of Sleep and Innovation Laboratories at the Center for BrainHealth, University of Texas at Dallas. This position plays a central role in enabling the efficient execution of the director’s academic, research, administrative, public outreach, and strategic responsibilities. The Adm... View Details Bookmark Senior Director of Development & Philanthropic Strategy S07187P CBH CR_Development Staff 08/07/2026 Driving visionary philanthropy to position Dallas as a global leader in brain health, resilience, and cognitive well-being.This position provides strategic leadership for a comprehensive development program driving transformational philanthropic support aligned with long-term priorities. Leads multi-year fundraising strategy and personally advances major and principal gifts. Serves as a key adv... View Details Bookmark Vice President for Enrollment Strategy S07186P Academic Affairs and Provost Dept Staff 08/07/2026 Position OverviewThe University of Texas at Dallas seeks an accomplished, visionary, and analytically sophisticated leader to serve as its next Vice President for Enrollment Strategy (VPES). Reporting directly to the Executive Vice President for Academic Affairs and Provost, the Vice President serves as the University’s chief architect of enrollment strategy, responsible for aligning enrollment... View Details Bookmark Part-Time Lecturer I & II (INTERNAL posting) F01125P Management Faculty 07/31/2027 04/09/2026 This internal posting is only to be used by internal applicants.Lecturers teach one or more undergraduate and/or graduate sections in a given term. Appointments carry no guarantee or expectation of renewal or tenure. View Details Bookmark Training Specialist S07075P CBH Chapman Staff 08/05/2026 Be the catalyst for student success and join us train more teachers withSMART! Early adolescence is an optimal time to enhance learning, but manyeducators do not have the benefit of scientific methods that foster theseskills. Our training program enables middle school throughninth grade teachers to take advantage of this important brain developmentstage and optimize student learning for success... View Details Bookmark Program Coordinator - Center for Global Business (JSOM) S07174P Management Staff 08/05/2026 The Program Coordinator plays a pivotal role in supporting the day-to-day coordination and execution of events, projects, and activities across the Center for Global Business (CGB)’s three core initiatives: the Global Talent & Mobility Initiative (GTMI), Global Development Initiative (GDI), and Future Leaders Initiative (FLI) within the Jindal School of Management (JSOM) at The University o... View Details Bookmark Previous 1 2 3 4 Next Human Resources, 800 West Campbell Road, AD3.418 Richardson, TX 75080-3021 972.883.2221 Check Us Out on Social Media To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at 