    "https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/all_jobs.atom": {
      "title": "The University Of Texas At Dallas: All Jobs",
      "description": "tag:jobs.utdallas.edu,2005:/postings/all_jobs The University Of Texas At Dallas: All Jobs 2026-06-11T15:53:30-05:00 https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32104 2026-06-11T15:53:30-05:00 2026-06-11T15:53:30-05:00 Finance Operations Coordinator <div>This position provides budgeting, finance, and procurement support for a medium to large complex department within the School of Engineering and Computer Science. Works closely with department faculty and staff to provide financial and research management and administration for the department’s finances, financial processes, and records to meet the department’s day-to-day financial operations goals. Assist in ensuring that compliance with all regulations, policies and university requirements are met to secure the department’s long-term financial viability and stability.</div> Mechanical Engineering https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32530 2026-08-26T09:52:40-05:00 2026-08-26T09:52:40-05:00 Part-time Lecturer - Mechanical Engineering <div>Lecturers teach one or more undergraduate and/or graduate sections in a given term. Appointments carry no guarantee or expectation of renewal or tenure.</div> Mechanical Engineering https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32379 2026-07-22T11:48:33-05:00 2026-07-22T11:48:34-05:00 Corporate Relations Specialist (JSOM) <div><strong>Job Summary</strong><br> The Corporate Relations Specialist (CRS) plays a key role in building and maintaining employer relationships for the Jindal School of Management (JSOM) at The University of Texas at Dallas. This position is responsible for assessing employer needs, developing strategies to support their recruiting efforts, and fostering long-term partnerships across a dynamic and evolving employer base.<br><br></div><div>Working closely with the Assistant Dean, Assistant Director of Corporate Relations, Corporate Relations Team, and Career Development Specialists, the CRS ensures all employer-related activities are effectively supported, tracked, and evaluated. The role provides critical support for engaging employers in major career events such as Career Expos, Employer Conferences, Industry Forums, Site Visits, Company Days, student organization career events, and information sessions. Additionally, the CRS manages key employer data, including postings, resume referrals, and participation metrics, to strengthen employer engagement and career services outcomes.</div> Management https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32516 2026-08-20T09:16:16-05:00 2026-08-20T09:16:17-05:00 Postdoctoral Research Associate <div>The Postdoctoral Research Associate will work as a research fellow within the Larynx Lab at the Texas Biomedical Device Center, supporting active projects in recovery from neurological injuries, vagus nerve stimulation, laryngeal dysfunction, and implantable neural devices, as well as developing their own ideas for new projects. Efforts will focus on working with pre-clinical models which facilitate translating the Center’s work into conducting pivotal research trials.</div> Texas Medical Device Center https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32346 2026-07-16T10:52:17-05:00 2026-07-16T10:52:18-05:00 Part Time Lecturer - JSOM Capstone Senior Projects <div>Lecturers teach one or more undergraduate and/or graduate sections in a given term. Appointments carry no guarantee or expectation of renewal or tenure.</div> Management https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32018 2026-06-02T10:30:42-05:00 2026-06-02T10:30:42-05:00 Temporary - NonBenefits Eligible (Archer Center) <div>The operations assistant provides direct candidate recruitment support to the Texas-based Archer Center team. This position assists with Archer Center recruitment by responding to prospective student questions, tracking interest in the program, following-up with interested students and researching new recruitment opportunities. The operations assistant will also be the coordinator and primary point person for Archer Fellow Alumni Ambassadors who assist with recruitment across the 14 University of Texas System institutions.<br><br></div><div>A successful candidate will be organized and detail-oriented, possess strong verbal and written communication skills, be poised and professional in representing the Archer Center, and handle confidential information with tact and discretion. This position requires a high level of organizational and time management skills and the ability to work with individuals from various academic institutions across the state. Travel is not required.<br><br></div><div>This position is based in The University of Texas System Administration Office/Archer Center in Austin, Texas, and reports to the Associate Director of Admissions and Campus Relations.</div> Honors College Dept https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32283 2026-07-07T16:29:19-05:00 2026-07-07T16:29:19-05:00 Audiology Clinical Extern <div>The 4th Year Extern Audiology scope of practice for this position will include; The performance of diagnostic and therapeutic audiological services on patients birth to adult who have, or wish to rule out hearing loss as the source of their communication disorders.<br><br>This would include hearing aid dispensing and fitting of assistive technology when appropriate. The performance of diagnostic vestibular evaluations on patients who wish to rule out peripheral vestibulopathy as the source of imbalance. The programming and diagnostic evaluation of pediatric cochlear implant patients.<br><br>All services will be provided under the supervision of a licensed audiologist serving as the 4th year Extern preceptor at the Callier-Dallas and Callier-Richardson locations.</div><div><br><strong>This position will start on June 1, 2027, and end on May 31, 2028.</strong></div> Callier Ctr Communication https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/31867 2026-05-11T09:34:01-05:00 2026-05-11T09:34:01-05:00 Research Associate <div>The research group led by Dr. You Leo Li at The University of Texas at Dallas is excited to invite applications for postdoctoral scholar positions. We're at the forefront of medical ultrasound imaging and artificial intelligence and look forward to welcoming ambitious new members to our team.<br><br>The research program of the group lies in the intersection of AI and medical ultrasound imaging. The paradigm shift towards the integration of AI and domain knowledge in ultrasound physics in medical ultrasound imaging is a recent yet promising development. Dr. Li's research program aims to harness this potential, focusing on AI- based quantitative imaging of human hemodynamics, as well as neural network models of nonlinear ultrasound for imaging and quantitative tissue property estimation. The outcome of these research projects could significantly enhance healthcare.<br><br>Successful applicants will have the opportunity to work with state-of-the-art ultrasound scanners, pioneer new imaging technologies, and collaborate with an array of imaging scientists at UT Dallas. Furthermore, our close partnership with the University of Texas Southwestern (UTSW) Medical Center allows for opportunities to engage in human studies. As part of our team, you will not only benefit from a dynamic and supportive research environment at UT Dallas and UTSW, but also from the vibrant culture of Dallas.</div> Bioengineering https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32494 2026-08-14T09:34:41-05:00 2026-08-14T09:34:41-05:00 Media Technology Specialist I <div>Under direct to general supervision, provides faculty, staff and students with technical support in the operation and set-up of media equipment. Provide professional and courteous instruction to faculty and staff in the proper use and handling of AV equipment. Will assist in maintaining a schedule of preventative maintenance. Must be dependable, reliable and be able to work both independently and as a team member.</div> Educational Technology Services https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32266 2026-07-06T14:36:22-05:00 2026-07-06T14:36:22-05:00 Part-time Lecturer - Media Arts and Design <div>Lecturers teach one or more undergraduate and/or graduate sections in a given term. Appointments carry no guarantee or expectation of renewal or tenure.</div> Arts, Humanities, and Technology https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/31528 2026-03-20T10:36:43-05:00 2026-03-20T10:36:43-05:00 Temporary Non Benefits- Child Development <div>This position supports the classroom teachers by carrying out daily tasks associated with caring for young children (0-5) such as diapering, feeding, supervising, playing, cleaning, etc.</div> Callier Ctr Communication https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32453 2026-08-06T08:23:09-05:00 2026-08-06T08:23:10-05:00 Part-Time Lecturer I & II (INTERNAL posting) <div>This internal posting is only to be used by internal applicants.<br><br>Lecturers teach one or more undergraduate and/or graduate sections in a given term. Appointments carry no guarantee or expectation of renewal or tenure.</div> Management https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/29871 2025-07-17T13:25:07-05:00 2025-07-17T13:25:08-05:00 Part-time Lecturer - Chemistry <div>Lecturers teach one or more undergraduate and/or graduate sections in a given term. Appointments carry no guarantee or expectation of renewal or tenure.</div> Chemistry https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32429 2026-07-31T15:57:34-05:00 2026-07-31T15:57:35-05:00 Graduation Specialist III <div><strong>Are you looking for a rewarding opportunity in higher education that provides a hybrid work schedule and a comprehensive benefits package with employee tuition assistance? Do you enjoy working in a collaborative and supportive environment?</strong></div><div><br></div><div><strong>The Office of the Registrar is looking for a detail-oriented individual with experience reviewing and analyzing records to fill the Graduation Specialist III position. Apply now to join our team!</strong></div><div><strong><br></strong>The Graduation Specialist III specializes in the in-depth examination and detailed analysis of student records and provides technical and academic customer service regarding the student record process. Reviews, analyzes, and performs complex calculations related to academic records and graduation, and is responsible for verification of student transfer data.</div> Office of the Registrar https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32231 2026-07-01T15:09:32-05:00 2026-07-01T15:09:32-05:00 Part-time Lecturer - Audiology or Speech/Language Pathology <div>The School of Behavioral and Brain Sciences is seeking part-time lecturers with expertise in speech-language pathology or audiology to teach undergraduate or graduate courses. Applicants with previous experience teaching should have a demonstrated record of teaching excellence.</div><div><br>This position will teach one or more undergraduate and/or graduate sections in a given term. Appointments carry no guarantee or expectation of renewal or tenure.<br><br></div><div>Applicants should upload a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy/experience (though not required), teaching evaluations (if available), and the full contact information for at least three academic or professional references; five (5) for those with no teaching experience.</div><div><br>Questions regarding this position can be sent to <a href=\"mailto:BBS.PeopleOps@utdallas.edu\"><strong>BBS.PeopleOps@utdallas.edu</strong></a></div> Speech Language Hearing https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32623 2026-09-04T13:47:23-05:00 2026-09-04T13:47:24-05:00 Head of Speech-Language Pathology <div>The Director of Speech-Language Pathology Clinical Operations at the Callier Center for Communication Disorders will be responsible for all clinical service activities in the Callier Speech-Language Pathology Clinic including overseeing scheduling, insurance and financial analyses for the clinic in collaboration with the Director of Business Operations and the Director of Administrative Operations.<br><br>The Director will also consult with Callier Center Leadership, including the Senior Director of Development on fund raising, clinical grant writing and marketing strategies for the speech-language pathology program. The successful candidate must be eligible for or hold a Texas License in Speech-Language Pathology and The Certificate of Clinical Competence (CCC-SLP) from the American Speech-Language and Hearing Association (ASHA).</div> Callier Ctr Communication https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32400 2026-07-27T08:13:26-05:00 2026-07-27T08:13:27-05:00 Development Associate <div>Reporting to the Jonsson School Assistant Dean of Development and Alumni Relations, this position supports the Assistant Dean and the Jonsson School development team. The successful candidate will work with the Jonsson School development and alumni relations team to support the activities of leadership annual giving and stewardship.<br><br>A successful candidate for this role will be excited to join the collaborative, open-minded and trust-filled environment that supports the development and alumni relations efforts of The University of Texas at Dallas and the Jonsson School of Engineering and Computer Science. This person should possess a high level of respect for all people and a customer service mentality that emphasizes the importance of relationships. The Development Associate will be intellectually curious and committed to continuously improving their leadership, skills, and knowledge.</div> Engineering & Computer Science https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32193 2026-06-25T11:39:38-05:00 2026-06-25T11:39:38-05:00 Postdoctoral Research Associate <div><br>The Romiti Group in the Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry at the University of Texas at Dallas, has a postdoctoral position available in the area of catalytic methods development and complex biologically active molecule synthesis. We are seeking a highly motivated and independent scientist with a strong background in organic synthesis and is excited about organic chemistry, synthesis and catalysis, to join our research team. Complex molecule synthesis experience is required. The postdoc will develop high-impact and practical catalytic transformations, and creative, novel synthesis strategies for the concise and efficient preparation of bioactive complex natural products and analogs thereof. The postdoc will also serve as a mentor to junior graduate students. The candidate should have completed a Ph.D. within the last three years or soon to be completed in chemistry or a related discipline.</div><div><br></div> Chemistry https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32562 2026-08-31T14:23:10-05:00 2026-08-31T14:23:10-05:00 Tax Accountant <div>The Tax Accountant reports to the Tax Compliance Manager and is responsible for the analysis, record keeping, payments, and reporting functions related to federal and state tax compliance. Responsibilities also include pension fund reconciliation and reporting, the completion of an annual UBIT analysis and private use survey, and communicating with tax authorities and individuals. Performs reconciliation and reclassification of payroll tax, benefits and pension liability accounts. The Tax Accountant analyzes and ensures the timely and accurate completion of tax related documentation and ensures full integration of the status determination into procurement and payroll processes according to applicable university, state, and federal standards.</div> Payroll https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32137 2026-06-17T14:59:27-05:00 2026-08-27T12:30:20-05:00 JSOM Administrative Support – FT Temporary <div>General support for a defined time period. Benefits Eligible.</div> Management https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32536 2026-08-27T08:40:50-05:00 2026-08-27T08:40:51-05:00 Financial Services Assistant <div>Works closely with department faculty and staff to provide financial and research management and administration for the department finances, financial processes, and records to meet the department's day-to-day financial operations goals. Assist in ensuring compliance with all regulations, policies, and university requirements are met to secure the department's long-term financial viability and stability. This position will serve the junior level of a two-tier structure for the finance and procurement team.</div> Computer Science https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32386 2026-07-23T09:55:42-05:00 2026-07-23T09:55:43-05:00 Part-time Lecturer - Criminology <div>Lecturers teach one or more undergraduate and/or graduate sections in a given term. Appointments carry no guarantee or expectation of renewal or tenure.</div> Criminology https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32034 2026-06-04T08:58:05-05:00 2026-06-04T08:58:06-05:00 Student Financial Aid Officer IV <div><strong>Are you interested in helping Veterans achieve their educational goals? Are you looking for a rewarding opportunity in higher education that provides a hybrid work schedule and a comprehensive benefits package with employee tuition benefits?<br><br>The Office of Financial Aid is seeking an individual with experience in Veterans' Education Benefits, student financial aid, student finance, or a related field to fill our Student Financial Aid Officer IV position. Apply now to join our team!</strong><br><br>The Student Financial Aid Officer IV reports to the Assistant Director of Financial Aid for Veterans' Education Benefits and serves as the School Certifying Officer. This position is responsible for processing student requests for Veterans' Education Benefits in compliance with all federal, state, and institutional rules and regulations and for assisting veteran and other military-connected students and families.</div> Office of Financial Aid https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32521 2026-08-23T11:20:31-05:00 2026-08-23T11:20:31-05:00 Associate Director - JSOM Career Management Center (CMC) <div>The <strong>Associate Director</strong> in the Jindal School of Management (JSOM) Career Management Center (CMC) is a strategic leader dedicated to advancing the career success of Undergraduate students. This role focuses exclusively on the undergraduate audience, designing and executing meaningful networking, internship, and career opportunities with employers actively seeking top talent. The position operates in a dynamic, fast-paced environment that emphasizes external engagement, relationship-building, and program leadership.<br><br></div><div>Reporting to the Assistant Dean of the Career Management Center, the Associate Director collaborates closely with the CMC team and has a direct impact on shaping student career outcomes and employer partnerships.</div> Management https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32374 2026-07-22T09:50:37-05:00 2026-07-22T09:50:37-05:00 Maintenance Worker - Building Envelope <div>Provide developing skills in surface preparation, application of different types of caulking and sealants, and detection and repair of water leaks on flat or metal roofs. Work with power tools and heavy equipment. Understand the basics of glazing windows. Replace ceiling tiles and ceiling grid. Repair or replace classrooms furniture. Repair or replace hardware in bathroom stalls.</div> Facilities Management https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32323 2026-07-13T18:16:38-05:00 2026-07-13T18:16:39-05:00 Research Administrator <div>The <strong>Research Administrator</strong> provides comprehensive pre-award and post-award support for research portfolios within the <strong>School of Behavioral and Brain Sciences (BBS)</strong>. This newly established position was created to formalize and strengthen research administration through a Grant Core model that embeds dedicated research support directly within academic departments.<br><br></div><div>Under this model, each department is supported by a full-time Research Administrator who reports directly to the Department Head and maintains a dotted-line relationship with the Sr. Director of Finance and Administration. This transition from a centrally managed structure to a department-based approach enables more specialized, responsive, and strategic support tailored to the unique needs of each department’s research portfolio.<br><br></div><div>The Research Administrator ensures compliance with University policies, sponsor guidelines, and federal regulations, including OMB 2 CFR 200 (Uniform Guidance), while providing support throughout the full lifecycle of sponsored projects—from proposal development and submission through award management and closeout. Through coordinated training, compliance oversight, quality assurance, and process improvement, the position advances the School’s research mission by promoting consistency, operational excellence, and high-quality service across all departments.</div> Psychology https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/31982 2026-05-27T11:20:47-05:00 2026-05-27T11:20:47-05:00 Pipefitter <div>Responsible for piping infrastructure involving water, air, steam, and various chemicals. Use stock and die or pipe threading machine in performance of work. Perform preventative maintenance related to water treatment. Connects and maintains all piping to pumps, tanks, vessels, etc. Maintains and replaces drain lines and steam traps. Demonstrate attention to details, resolve routine problems, and follow procedures and instructions. Inspects and oversees contractor work. Position includes work inside cramped or confined spaces.</div> Facilities Management https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32502 2026-08-14T16:40:41-05:00 2026-08-14T16:40:42-05:00 Payroll Specialist I <div>Under the general direction of the Payroll Manager, the Payroll Specialist I provides technical skills required in the processing of payrolls and related data within a highly technical payroll system. Responsible for preparing and submitting payrolls and related monthly reports.<br><br>The Payroll Specialist I is responsible for ensuring that all time and labor setup is complete for new and existing employees, timesheet data is accurate and reported timely, payrolls are processed accurately, all adjustments are properly entered, and accounting entries are processed for month-end closes. Other responsibilities may include reconciliation of deductions, tax data, and balance sheet account transactions.</div> Payroll https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32268 2026-07-06T15:02:42-05:00 2026-07-06T15:02:42-05:00 Part-time Lecturer - History and Philosophy <div>Lecturers teach one or more undergraduate and/or graduate sections in a given term. Appointments carry no guarantee or expectation of renewal or tenure.</div> Arts, Humanities, and Technology https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/31809 2026-04-29T09:39:44-05:00 2026-04-29T09:39:45-05:00 Research Associate <div>Biomedical Micro Devices and Nanotechnology Lab seeks to hire a Postdoctoral Researcher to spearhead the development of innovative diagnostic biosensors. The successful candidate will focus on the end-to-end pipeline of biomarker discovery and sensor engineering, from molecular selection to high-fidelity analytical validation.<br><br></div><div>Key responsibilities and required expertise include:</div><ul><li>Aptamer Discovery &amp; SELEX: Mastery of SELEX (Systematic Evolution of Ligands by Exponential Enrichment) methodologies to identify, select, and optimize high-affinity DNA/RNA aptamers for novel biomarker targets. Experience in post-SELEX characterization (e.g., determining Kd values) is essential.</li><li>Biomarker Analysis (LC/MS): Proficiency in using LC/MS (Liquid Chromatography-Mass Spectrometry) to characterize and quantify biomarkers within complex biological matrices such as sweat, saliva, or blood, facilitating the transition from discovery to detection.</li><li>Sensor Design &amp; Engineering: A strong understanding of biochemistry and materials chemistry to integrate custom-developed aptamers into functional biosensor platforms (e.g., electrochemical).</li></ul><div><br></div><div>Assay Development: The ability to independently design and execute complex, novel assay protocols for multiple biomarkers, ensuring robustness and sensitivity in real-world samples.</div> Bioengineering https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32462 2026-08-07T13:53:11-05:00 2026-08-07T13:53:12-05:00 Senior Director of Development & Philanthropic Strategy <div>Driving visionary philanthropy to position Dallas as a global leader in brain health, resilience, and cognitive well-being.<strong><br></strong><br></div><div>This position provides strategic leadership for a comprehensive development program driving transformational philanthropic support aligned with long-term priorities. Leads multi-year fundraising strategy and personally advances major and principal gifts. Serves as a key advisor to leadership, drives cross-institutional alignment, and cultivates high-level donor relationships while elevating visibility and building a high-performing development function positioned for sustained growth.<br><br></div><div><strong>Take the next step in your career with a rewarding and challenging opportunity at Center for BrainHealth. Join a team dedicated to advancing groundbreaking research, education, and community impact. Apply now!</strong></div> CBH CR_Development https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/31069 2026-01-07T09:58:39-06:00 2026-01-07T09:58:40-06:00 Building Attendant II - Porter <div>This position will provide general maintenance and custodial support for UTD’s Student Housing facilities. Duties involve general support of an assigned housing building.</div> Housing Operations https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32443 2026-08-04T10:18:09-05:00 2026-08-04T10:18:09-05:00 Director – UTDSolv (JSOM) <div>The <strong>Director of Industry Projects</strong> plays a pivotal leadership role in advancing the mission of <strong>UTDSolv at the UT Dallas Jindal School of Management</strong> by developing, managing, and scaling a dynamic portfolio of industry-sponsored projects that deliver meaningful, high-impact experiential learning opportunities for students. This role serves as the primary liaison between UTDSolv and industry organizations to identify, scope, and secure applied projects that align with academic objectives and workforce needs.<br><br>The Director oversees the full project lifecycle—from project sourcing and scoping through execution, assessment, and reporting—while ensuring positive outcomes for students, faculty, and industry partners. This position is responsible for maintaining a robust project pipeline, managing project quality, monitoring student performance, and measuring the impact of UTDSolv initiatives.</div> Management https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32238 2026-07-02T08:49:46-05:00 2026-07-02T08:49:46-05:00 Part-time Lecturer - Electrical and Computer Engineering <div>Lecturers teach one or more undergraduate and/or graduate sections in a given term. Appointments carry no guarantee or expectation of renewal or tenure.</div> Electrical and Computer Engineering https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32406 2026-07-28T10:30:31-05:00 2026-07-28T10:30:31-05:00 Postdoctoral Research Associate <div>The Center for Wind Energy at UT Dallas (UTD Wind) seeks to fill a research associate position aimed at increasing annual energy production (AEP) on wind farms. The position is to support a two-year Small Business Technology Transfer project (STTR) funded by the National Science Foundation. The successful candidate is expected to support the development, simulation and testing of model-free algorithms for real-time optimization of turbine operating conditions (e.g., yaw set points). Other projects may be assigned by the supervisor depending on skills and technical needs.<br><br>The successful candidate will be part of a team of faculty members, graduate students, and industry partners developing methodology and new technologies for wind energy systems. The successful candidate is expected to assist in the supervision of graduate students and publish scientific papers. Participation in the development of sponsored research is encouraged. UTD Wind is home to a site of WindSTAR, an NSF Industry/University Cooperative Research Center for use-inspired R&amp;D to advance wind energy science &amp; technology. UTD Wind is also a member of the Ocean Safety Energy Institute (OESI), a consortium of industry, national labs, non-governmental organizations based at Texas A&amp;M Engineering Experiment Station, and the European Academy of Wind Energy (EAWE). UT Dallas is co-hosting the 2025 NAWEA/WindTech Conference in the metroplex.<br><br></div> Mechanical Engineering https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32202 2026-06-26T15:12:24-05:00 2026-06-26T15:12:25-05:00 Postdoctoral Research Associate <div>The Jiang Lab at the University of Texas at Dallas is seeking multiple postdoctoral researchers in the area of protein-based therapeutics. Our research focuses on the design of novel proteins/antibodies and explore their biomedical applications. Our goal is to utilize these engineered proteins to precisely regulate intracellular signaling pathways, eventually translating these toolkits into biotechnology platforms and therapeutic reagents. Our research program integrates chemical biology, protein engineering, and cell biology techniques for therapeutic development. Candidates with expertise in cell biology, genome engineering, CRISPR-based screening, functional genomics, or <em>C. elegans</em> genetics are particularly encouraged to apply.<br><br></div><div><br></div> Chemistry https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32568 2026-09-01T10:41:09-05:00 2026-09-01T10:41:10-05:00 Child Development Specialist III - Preschool <div><strong>Looking for a rewarding opportunity to work with children? Join our Callier Center Team!<br><br></strong>The Callier Center provides a nurturing, learning environment for infants through kindergarten Age. We focus on developing every child’s specific needs, including communication and language skills, physical abilities, emotional and social growth and cognitive development. Our Program fosters an environment in which children have the opportunity to communicate, play and develop friendships with other children whose interests, abilities, levels of hearing and methods of communication may be different than their own.<br><br>Provide comprehensive developmental programs for preschool populations; provide periodic developmental assessment for preschool ages, and provide model/demonstration services such as parent consultation, quality child care, and on-site university training; provide leadership to teaching teams in a preschool setting.</div> Callier Ctr Communication https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32142 2026-06-18T10:12:47-05:00 2026-06-18T10:12:47-05:00 Part-Time Lecturer - Mathematical Sciences <div>Lecturers teach one or more undergraduate and/or graduate sections in a given term. Appointments carry no guarantee or expectation of renewal or tenure.<br><br>Applicants should upload a curriculum vitae.<br><br></div> Mathematical Sciences https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32558 2026-08-28T13:44:55-05:00 2026-08-28T13:44:55-05:00 Open-Rank Non-Tenure System Faculty position - Clinical Professor/Professor of Practice and Program Director <div><strong>Position Description</strong></div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>The Naveen Jindal School of Management is seeking a non-tenure track Clinical Professor/Professor of Practice and Program Director to lead the Alliance for Physician Leadership (APL) program, a nationally recognized Healthcare Leadership &amp; Management Executive MS/MBA exclusively for physician leaders.&nbsp; The program’s over 750 physician graduates currently occupy senior healthcare leadership roles throughout the United States.&nbsp; APL also offers healthcare certificate programs in partnership with healthcare systems for their emerging physician leaders. Appointment will be at the Assistant, Associate or full Professor rank, depending on experience.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>The Program Director’s role will be to collaborate with healthcare system leaders to assure program alignment with industry needs. The role collaborates on recruitment and selection of physicians and preservation of the program’s strong, supportive culture. The incumbent will also be expected to play an active role in program design and teaching; assuring program quality and financial success; coaching and mentoring aspiring physician leaders; recruiting and retaining appropriate faculty; and managing program staff. Extensive experience in healthcare leadership and operations and familiarity with current physician leadership issues are essential for this role.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>The successful candidate will be responsible for teaching graduate classes in Healthcare Administration. Curriculum oversight and ensuring that AACSB, university and school requirements are achieved, contributing assessment information and data as requested with an emphasis in sustainable practices.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>The preferred starting date is November 2026, teaching duties commence for the spring 2027 semester.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong>Qualifications</strong></div><div><strong>&nbsp;</strong></div><div>Minimum Education and Experience: A MS or equivalent in Healthcare Administration, Medical Management or a related discipline is required prior to employment. Candidates are expected to demonstrate the ability to work effectively in a highly collaborative, engaging, and dynamic environment comprised of individuals with a range of backgrounds, skills, and perspectives. We are seeking candidates able to deliver high quality teaching using evidence-based practices to effectively engage students from a range of backgrounds and experiences.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Preferred Education and Experience: PhD, MD or DO in Healthcare Administration, Medical Management or a related field. Substantial industry experience (at least five to ten years) in healthcare administration and familiarity with current physician leadership issues is strongly preferred and will weigh heavily in the review process.</div><div><strong>&nbsp;</strong></div><div><strong>The Department</strong></div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>The UT Dallas Executive Education area focuses on the education of working professionals through specialized corporate programs or certificate and degree options including Executive MBA and Executive MS options. &nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Degree emphasis and certificate topics include global marketing, healthcare, leadership, organizational consulting, project management, strategy, strategic human resources, supply chain. Corporate programs are typically customized to meet the needs of the client. &nbsp;</div><div><strong>&nbsp;</strong></div><div><strong>The Naveen Jindal School of Management</strong></div><div><strong>&nbsp;</strong></div><div>The Naveen Jindal School of Management has become a national and international leader in research and education since its own entrepreneurial beginning in 1975. Over 10,000 undergraduate and graduate students are enrolled in the Jindal School, the largest and fastest growing school at UT Dallas. With over 30 programs, we boast a diverse faculty and student body that provide an inclusive fusion of cultures and experiences.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong>Application Instructions</strong></div><div><strong>&nbsp;</strong></div><div>Applicants should upload the following:<a href=\"https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32549\"><strong> </strong></a><strong>&nbsp;</strong></div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>·&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Full curriculum vitae and cover letter summarizing their interests and qualifications for the position.</div><div>·&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Statement of teaching philosophy describing their conceptualizations of teaching and learning, and teaching and assessment methods, and how their teaching practices will engage students from a range of backgrounds and experiences.</div><div>·&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Full contact information for at least three academic or professional references.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Priority will be given to completed applications received by September 14, 2026. Reviews will continue until the position is filled or the search is closed on September 30, 2026.</div><div><strong>&nbsp;</strong></div><div><strong>The University and Community&nbsp;<br></strong><br></div><div>UT Dallas is a top public research university located in one of the nation’s fastest-growing metropolitan regions. Our seven schools offer 160 undergraduate and graduate degree programs, plus undergraduate and graduate certificates. Our student body is around 30,000 strong, reflecting students from over 100 countries and a multiplicity of perspectives and experiences. Over 60% of our undergraduate students receive some form of need- or merit-based financial aid, and 62% of graduating seniors have no student debt compared to 49% in all Texas publics and 51% in all national publics (<a href=\"https://www.utdallas.edu/about-us/fast-facts/\"><strong>UT Dallas Fast Facts</strong></a>).&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>Under the dynamic leadership of President Prabhas V. Moghe, UT Dallas is charting a path built on three strategic pillars – student success, academic and research convergence, and external impact. Guided by the <a href=\"https://roadmap.utdallas.edu/\"><strong>Roadmap 2030</strong></a> plan, UT Dallas will accelerate its upward trajectory to become a university of even greater impact and distinction.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>UT Dallas is committed to graduating well-rounded members of the community whose education has prepared them for rewarding lives and productive careers in a constantly changing world. Our mission centers on providing Texas and the nation with excellent and innovative education and research. The University’s rapid growth is fueled by our creative and enterprising spirt, bright students, innovative programs, renowned faculty, dedicated staff, engaged alumni, and research that matters.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>The University promotes a welcoming environment through programs and initiatives designed to support engagement and success for members of the campus community. Employee benefits include a range of physical and mental wellness resources, competitive insurance and retirement plan options, lactation facilities located throughout the campus, and Employee Resource Groups (ERGs) comprised of individuals who share common interests to help build community among UT Dallas faculty and staff (e.g., Universal Access ERG, Military and Veteran ERG, UT Dallas Young Professionals). Additionally, the University’s modern campus, 400+ campus organizations, and prime location foster collaboration and community.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Situated in Richardson, Texas, the University’s location offers abundant professional development and entertainment options. The Dallas-Fort Worth (DFW) metroplex is rich with visual and performing arts venues, museum districts, professional and semi-professional athletics teams, botanical gardens, accessible trails, and much more, ensuring there’s something for everyone. The University’s partnerships with regional higher education institutions, local school districts, numerous companies, and the Richardson Innovation Quarter (Richardson IQ) – a major hub for innovation, entrepreneurship, and educational activities – promotes collaboration, professional growth, and educational excellence.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong>Equal Employment Opportunity<br></strong><br> The University of Texas at Dallas is committed to providing an educational, living and working environment that is welcoming, respectful, and inclusive of all members of the university community. The University <a href=\"https://policy.utdallas.edu/utdbp3090\"><strong>prohibits unlawful discrimination</strong></a> against a person because of their race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, or veteran status.</div> Executive Education https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32391 2026-07-23T13:54:31-05:00 2026-07-23T13:54:31-05:00 Student Program Coordinator <div>Under the supervision of the Living Learning Communities (LLC) Assistant Director, provide program assistance to assigned communities. Duties include: developing and facilitating evening, weekend, in-person, and virtual programs; developing and maintaining faculty partnerships; facilitating marketing initiatives including social media; assisting in assessment; conducting academic intervention; managing application process; and tracking course enrollment.</div> Residential Life https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32077 2026-06-09T08:40:44-05:00 2026-06-09T08:40:45-05:00 Research Scientist - DILLON / DENISCO Lab <div>The Dillon and De Nisco laboratories are looking to hire a co-mentored postdoctoral scholar to work on collaborative projects on improving antibiotic outcomes in urinary tract infection management. The Dillon lab seeks to decipher the basis for how antibiotic resistance evolves, specializing in research on high-priority MDR pathogens, antibiotic pharmacology, and host-pathogen interactions including murine models of infection. Our current focus is how we can modify the host microenvironment to improve antibiotic efficacies.<br><br>The De Nisco lab is focused on understanding mechanisms of microbial pathogenesis, host response, and urinary microbiome structure and function contributing to recurrent urinary tract infection (rUTI) in postmenopausal women. A current major research focus of the De Nisco lab is the role of the urinary microenvironment in UTI susceptibility and treatment outcomes. We seek to understand how the female urinary tract is shaped by aging, hormonal status, and history of infection using metagenomics, advanced statistical models, and analytical biochemistry.<br><br></div><div><em>This position will be co-mentored by two TT Faculty in two different laboratories.</em></div> Biological Sciences https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32528 2026-08-25T08:47:23-05:00 2026-08-25T08:47:23-05:00 Program Specialist II <div>The position is responsible for providing expertise to implement, develop, and evaluate enrollment initiatives, develop recruitment strategies, and assist the department of Interdisciplinary Studies with strategic implementation of recruitment activities by identifying strong recruitment approaches and developing outreach programs.</div> Interdisciplinary Studies https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32378 2026-07-22T11:47:50-05:00 2026-07-22T11:47:50-05:00 Career Development Specialist (JSOM) <div>The <strong>Career Development Specialist (CDS) </strong>for the JSOM Career Management Center (CMC) plays a vital role in preparing undergraduate students for career success. This position provides personalized coaching in résumé development, networking, LinkedIn optimization, cover letter writing, mock interviews, and internship search strategies.<br><br></div><div>The CDS will meet with students individually, lead professional development workshops, conduct classroom presentations, and collaborate with undergraduate programs and concentrations to ensure students are career-ready.<br><br></div><div>Reporting to the Associate Director of Undergraduate Professional Development, the CDS will work closely with the Assistant Dean, Corporate Relations Team, and other Career Development Specialists to deliver comprehensive career support. As an active member of the CMC team, this role will also assist with student engagement initiatives, employer events, and other center activities as needed.<br><br></div><div><strong>Please Note:</strong> There are <strong>two vacancies</strong> for this position.</div> Management https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32504 2026-08-17T10:48:05-05:00 2026-08-17T10:48:05-05:00 Media Technology Specialist II <div>This position supports the preparation, setup, operation, maintenance, troubleshooting, and continued advancement of the university's immersive projection classroom and its Pixera-based visualization environment. Working closely with the lead technician assigned to the immersive classroom, this position assists with classroom operations, preventative maintenance, technical support, and instructional activities while developing expertise in immersive visualization technologies and advanced audiovisual systems.<br><br>The position assists in diagnosing and resolving technical issues, performs preventative maintenance, and helps ensure the reliable operation of the immersive classroom while supporting courses utilizing the immersive projection system. Working collaboratively with faculty, staff, and the lead technician assigned to the immersive classroom, this position provides technical support, production assistance, and classroom operational support while gaining experience with the design, implementation, and delivery of immersive instructional technologies.<br><br>Under direct to general supervision provide faculty, staff and students with technical assistance, support, and policy and procedure orientation on media equipment capabilities and operations.</div> Educational Technology Services https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32343 2026-07-15T19:20:15-05:00 2026-07-15T19:20:16-05:00 Senior Manager, Outreach and Recruitment <div><br>The Senior Manager for the UT Dallas Latin America Office serves as the university’s primary representative in the region, responsible for advancing institutional partnerships, supporting strategic international enrollment initiatives, and enhancing student engagement across Latin America. This role is designed for an experienced higher education professional with direct experience working with universities in the United States or with institutions that have strong knowledge of the U.S. higher education system.<br><br></div><div>The Senior Manager engages prospective students, families, secondary schools, universities, counselors, and other educational partners to support UT Dallas’s international enrollment and expansion efforts. Working closely with UT Dallas admissions, academic units, and International Center staff, the role advances enrollment strategy and institutional priorities, represents the university at targeted events, and contributes to the development of institutional partnerships.<br><br></div><div>A key responsibility of this position is to support enrollment yield through sustained engagement with admitted students. This includes responding to inquiries, facilitating pre-arrival advising and communications, and supporting events and initiatives that help students successfully transition from admission to enrollment<br><br></div><div>The Senior Manager will also strengthen relationships with UT Dallas alumni in the region and identify opportunities for alumni engagement in student outreach and recruitment activities. Regular visits to the UT Dallas campus are expected to maintain a strong understanding of institutional priorities, academic offerings, and the student experience.<br><br></div><div>Given the independent nature of this role, the successful candidate will demonstrate strong professional judgment, self-direction, and the ability to manage relationships, events, and communications with minimal day-to-day supervision. This role requires confidence in representing UT Dallas publicly and the ability to build long-term relationships that advance the university’s visibility, enrollment, and student success in Latin America.<br><br></div><div>This full-time position is based in Mexico City, Mexico, via contract with Safeguard Global, and includes regional and international travel. Responsibilities also include office and project management, periodic facilitation of seminars and workshops, and presentations at conferences and programs.</div><div><br></div> International Center https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/31986 2026-05-27T11:24:01-05:00 2026-05-27T11:24:01-05:00 HVAC Technician <div>Performs preventative maintenance on HVAC equipment, this includes changing air filters, greasing, replacement of belts, etc. Installs motors, electronics, thermostats, humidistats, fans, other HVAC components, heating water and hydronics, chilled water controls and automated control systems. Assists with troubleshooting and resolving issues with HVAC equipment. Maintain a flexible work schedule including being on-call. Other duties as assigned. Must be willing to work weekends. This position will be located at our Dallas location: 2126 W Mockingbird Ln Dallas, TX 75235.</div> Facilities Management https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32270 2026-07-06T15:50:50-05:00 2026-07-06T15:50:51-05:00 Part-time Lecturer - Visual and Performing Arts <div>Lecturers teach one or more undergraduate and/or graduate sections in a given term. Appointments carry no guarantee or expectation of renewal or tenure.</div> Arts, Humanities, and Technology https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/31857 2026-05-07T08:45:26-05:00 2026-05-07T08:45:26-05:00 Research Technician - SHUKLA Lab <div>&nbsp;<br>The <a href=\"https://labs.utdallas.edu/shukla/\"><strong>Shukla Lab</strong></a> at the University of Texas at Dallas is seeking a research technician to join a new research program studying the role of biological membranes in neurodegeneration, aging, and cancer.</div><div><br>Our work integrates membrane biophysics, protein biochemistry, and cell biology to uncover how membrane damage and repair processes influence cellular function and disease progression. We combine biochemical reconstitution, quantitative fluorescence microscopy, and cell-based approaches to study membrane-associated mechanisms at molecular and cellular scales.</div><div><br>We are seeking a motivated scientist with strong training in molecular biology, biochemistry, or cell biology. The successful candidate will contribute to ongoing research projects while also supporting laboratory operations in a collaborative and intellectually engaging research environment.&nbsp; We are looking for individuals who are curious, rigorous, and collaborative.<br><br>Members of the Shukla Lab are encouraged to think critically about experiments, engage in scientific discussion, and contribute ideas that help shape ongoing research. Early members of the lab will play an important role in helping establish experimental platforms and building a collaborative scientific environment.&nbsp;</div><div><br>The initial appointment will be for one year but can be renewed based on performance and fit within the lab.<br><br></div> Biological Sciences https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32480 2026-08-12T10:38:57-05:00 2026-08-12T10:38:57-05:00 Lab Manager <div>The Price Lab is seeking to hire a Laboratory Manager to be responsible for overseeing and supervising laboratory personnel, ensuring adherence to safety protocols, managing lab resources, and overseeing daily operations. This role requires strong leadership, organizational skills, and technical expertise to maintain high-quality standards in laboratory practices.<br><br></div><div>The Price Laboratory, at UT Dallas, is interested in the fundamental principles underlying neuronal plasticity leading to chronic pain. We aim to develop novel therapeutics based on these discoveries with the potential to either prevent the development of or permanently reverse chronic pain states. We focus on two major areas: plasticity in peripheral nociceptive neurons following injury and plasticity in central nervous system circuits that result from persistent stimulation of peripheral nociceptors. We utilize molecular, biochemical, genetic, behavioral, imaging and electrophysiological techniques combined with an overarching interest in pharmacology and drug discovery to tackle this problem.</div><div><br></div><div><em>This is an NIH grant funded position, and continued employment is contingent on the availability of funds.</em></div> Neuroscience https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/31264 2026-02-10T15:44:03-06:00 2026-02-10T15:44:04-06:00 Temporary-Part-Time Food Services <div>We are seeking a dependable and well‑organized Part‑Time Food Services team member to join the Callier Child Development Program. This role is essential in supporting daily meal preparation and maintaining a clean, safe, and efficient kitchen environment. Key responsibilities include assisting with the preparation of nutritious meals and snacks, upholding high standards of hygiene and cleanliness, and ensuring full compliance with food safety regulations. <strong><em>This temporary, non‑benefits‑eligible position is scheduled for 19.5 hours per week.</em></strong></div> Callier Ctr Communication https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32448 2026-08-05T11:43:57-05:00 2026-08-05T11:43:58-05:00 Training Specialist <div>Be the catalyst for student success and join us train more teachers with<br>SMART! Early adolescence is an optimal time to enhance learning, but many<br>educators do not have the benefit of scientific methods that foster these<br>skills. Our training program enables middle school through<br>ninth grade teachers to take advantage of this important brain development<br>stage and optimize student learning for success in the classroom and<br>beyond. The Training Specialist will provide technical skills to train teachers in<br>the classroom to carry out SMART training techniques. Responsible for<br>coordinating procedures and performing additional lab-related duties in<br>accordance with needs for data processing and coding.</div> CBH Chapman https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32261 2026-07-06T11:58:54-05:00 2026-07-06T11:58:55-05:00 Part-time Lecturer - Animation and Games <div>Lecturers teach one or more undergraduate and/or graduate sections in a given term. Appointments carry no guarantee or expectation of renewal or tenure.</div> Arts, Humanities, and Technology https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32424 2026-07-30T18:32:33-05:00 2026-07-30T18:32:33-05:00 Program Specialist I <div>Provide administrative, human resources, and payroll support for a medium to large workload in the Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering within the Jonsson School of Engineering and Computer Science</div> Electrical and Computer Engineering https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32230 2026-07-01T14:57:35-05:00 2026-07-01T14:57:35-05:00 Part-time Lecturer - Psychology <div>The School of Behavioral and Brain Sciences is seeking part-time lecturers with expertise in Psychology to teach undergraduate or graduate courses. Applicants with previous experience teaching should have a demonstrated record of teaching excellence.</div><div><br>This position will teach one or more undergraduate and/or graduate sections in a given term. Appointments carry no guarantee or expectation of renewal or tenure.</div><div><br>Applicants should upload a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy/experience (though not required), teaching evaluations (if available), and the full contact information for at least three academic or professional references; five (5) for those with no teaching experience.</div><div><br>Questions regarding this position can be sent to <a href=\"mailto:BBS.PeopleOps@utdallas.edu\"><strong>BBS.PeopleOps@utdallas.edu</strong></a></div> Psychology https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32609 2026-09-02T14:51:54-05:00 2026-09-02T14:51:54-05:00 Lab Technician / Research Assistant <div>The Department of Neuroscience at UT Dallas has an opening for a Laboratory Technician/Research Assistant to join the Tavares Lab. The lab studies the cellular and molecular mechanisms underlying pain, peripheral neuropathies, and neurodegenerative diseases. Our research uses animal models, cell culture, molecular and histological approaches, and transcriptomic analyses to better understand mechanisms of nerve dysfunction and disease.</div><div><br>The Laboratory Technician/Research Assistant will provide technical and research support for ongoing laboratory projects, with a primary emphasis on animal studies of pain and peripheral neuropathy. The position will also provide opportunities to contribute to cell culture, tissue processing, microscopy, molecular biology, and transcriptomic studies. Experience working with rodents is preferred. Training will be provided for specialized techniques. <br><br><strong>This position is particularly well suited for a recent graduate seeking post-baccalaureate research experience before pursuing a PhD or other graduate training.<br></strong><br></div><div><em>This position may be fully or in part funded by a grant. Continued employment is contingent on the availability of funds and satisfactory performance.</em></div> Neuroscience https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32399 2026-07-24T13:52:49-05:00 2026-07-24T13:52:50-05:00 Child Development Associate - Infant/Toddler <div><strong>Looking for a rewarding opportunity to work with children?<br>Join our Callier Center Team!<br><br></strong>The Callier Center provides a nurturing, learning environment for infants through kindergarten Age. We focus on developing every child’s specific needs, including communication and language skills, physical abilities, emotional and social growth, and cognitive development. Our Program fosters an environment in which children have the opportunity to communicate, play, and develop friendships with other children whose interests, abilities, levels of hearing and methods of communication may be different than their own.<br><br>Provide assistance in the provision of developmental program activities for young children focusing on the infant/toddler age group by providing care and developmentally appropriate experiences for infant/toddler age children; maintain a safe and appropriate learning environment; work collaboratively with team members in planning and implementing activities; document observations of individual child development; provide daily verbal and written communication to parents.</div> Callier Ctr Communication https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32155 2026-06-22T16:22:25-05:00 2026-06-22T16:22:26-05:00 Student Financial Aid Officer II <div><strong>Are you interested in helping students achieve their educational and professional goals? Are you looking for a rewarding opportunity in higher education that provides a hybrid remote work schedule and a comprehensive benefits package including employee tuition assistance?<br><br>If so, apply now to join our team!<br></strong><br>The Student Financial Aid Officer II performs a variety of job duties associated with the coordination, awarding, disbursement, and returning of state, federal and institutional financial aid assistance programs as part of the Office of Financial Aid Counseling and Customer Service Team. This position advises students and families about financial aid processes and requirements, collaborates with other University departments to promote a positive student experience, and works with other Office of Financial Aid teams to ensure efficient and accurate processing of financial aid.</div> Office of Financial Aid https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32561 2026-08-31T08:48:09-05:00 2026-08-31T08:48:10-05:00 LARC Technician <div>To assist in the maintenance and operation of the animal experimentation/research facilities. Responsible for the performance of routine non-technical tasks.<br><br>The training schedule for the Animal Technician is M-F, 8am-5pm. Once adequate training is accomplished (a few weeks depending on experience) new technicians are required to work the weekends and take 2 days off during the week.</div> Research Operations & Labs https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32133 2026-06-17T09:32:18-05:00 2026-06-17T09:32:18-05:00 Application Administrator IV <div>The Digital Content Services (DCS) team supports enterprise content management, workflow automation, and integrated digital business solutions that enable academic and administrative units to modernize operations, improve efficiency, and support strategic institutional initiatives.<br><br>This position serves as a senior enterprise application administrator and technical lead for Hyland OnBase and associated enterprise content management and workflow automation platforms. The role is responsible for the architectural design, administration, integration, lifecycle management, governance, optimization, and operational support of enterprise applications and related services supporting mission-critical university operations.<br><br>This position provides technical leadership for enterprise workflow automation, document management, intelligent document processing, and system integration initiatives involving platforms such as PeopleSoft, Salesforce, identity management services, and other university enterprise systems. Responsibilities include designing and supporting complex integrations, establishing technical standards and best practices, leading system upgrades and modernization efforts, troubleshooting complex enterprise application issues, and identifying opportunities to expand enterprise platform capabilities across campus.<br><br>The position collaborates closely with campus stakeholders, vendors, project teams, and IT leadership to support strategic digital transformation initiatives, improve operational efficiency, and maximize the university’s return on investment in enterprise application platforms.<br><br>This position also provides mentoring, technical guidance, and knowledge transfer to team members and serves as a senior escalation point for complex enterprise application and integration issues.</div> Information Technology-Digital Transformation https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32532 2026-08-26T15:26:09-05:00 2026-08-26T15:26:10-05:00 Assistant Director for Facilities Services <div>Responsible for the management of the Main Campus facilities services operations and programs (Custodial, Grounds, Garage, Signs &amp; Keys, Move &amp; Events, and Maintenance &amp; Construction). Shares responsibility with another Assistant Director for the management of department operations in the absence of the Director of Facilities Services &amp; Operations.</div> Facilities Management https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32384 2026-07-23T09:32:59-05:00 2026-07-23T09:32:59-05:00 Part-time Lecturer - Systems Engineering <div>Lecturers teach one or more undergraduate and/or graduate sections in a given term. Appointments carry no guarantee or expectation of renewal or tenure.</div> System Engineering https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32519 2026-08-21T11:56:06-05:00 2026-08-21T11:56:06-05:00 Academic Advisor II <div>Academic advisors provide specialized academic advising services to students and advising-based perspectives to University colleagues and public stakeholders, such as students, family-members and prospective students. By integrating excellent interpersonal and communication skills with knowledge or curricula, policies (departmental, School, and University), resources, and student development, the Advisor helps students identify options, set academic and developmental goals, and make progress toward those goals.<br><br>The advisor assists in the development or advising programs and initiatives that facilitate student engagement, success, and retention, provides advising data, and collaborates with academic and other University operational units on matters that impact student recruitment, success, and retention.<br><br></div> NSM Deans Office https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32372 2026-07-22T09:48:25-05:00 2026-07-22T09:48:26-05:00 Irrigation Technician <div>Under general supervision, the Irrigation Technician installs, inspects, renovates, and maintains irrigation systems for the University.</div> Facilities Management https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32030 2026-06-04T08:52:28-05:00 2026-06-04T08:52:29-05:00 Student Financial Aid Officer III <div><strong>Are you interested in helping Veterans achieve their educational and professional goals? Are you looking for a rewarding opportunity in higher education that provides a hybrid work schedule and a comprehensive benefits package including employee tuition assistance? Apply now to join our team!</strong></div><div><br></div><div><strong>The Office of Financial Aid is looking for an individual with veterans' education benefits, student financial aid, or related experience to fill our Student Financial Aid Officer III position.</strong></div><div><br></div><div>The Student Financial Aid Officer III reports to the Assistant Director of the Veterans' Benefits Team and is responsible for verifying, processing, awarding, disbursing, and providing customer service support to students and staff related to the Hazlewood Act exemption at UT Dallas.</div> Office of Financial Aid https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32322 2026-07-13T18:16:16-05:00 2026-07-13T18:16:17-05:00 Research Administrator <div>The <strong>Research Administrator</strong> provides comprehensive pre-award and post-award support for research portfolios within the <strong>School of Behavioral and Brain Sciences (BBS)</strong>. This newly established position was created to formalize and strengthen research administration through a Grant Core model that embeds dedicated research support directly within academic departments.<br><br></div><div>Under this model, each department is supported by a full-time Research Administrator who reports directly to the Department Head and maintains a dotted-line relationship with the Sr. Director of Finance and Administration. This transition from a centrally managed structure to a department-based approach enables more specialized, responsive, and strategic support tailored to the unique needs of each department’s research portfolio.<br><br></div><div>The Research Administrator ensures compliance with University policies, sponsor guidelines, and federal regulations, including OMB 2 CFR 200 (Uniform Guidance), while providing support throughout the full lifecycle of sponsored projects—from proposal development and submission through award management and closeout. Through coordinated training, compliance oversight, quality assurance, and process improvement, the position advances the School’s research mission by promoting consistency, operational excellence, and high-quality service across all departments.</div><div><br></div> Speech Language Hearing https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/31978 2026-05-27T11:16:05-05:00 2026-05-27T11:16:06-05:00 Electrician Journeyman <div><strong>Looking for a rewarding career opportunity with great benefits? Look no further! Join our team!</strong><br><br>To provide journeyman level skills and expertise in the installation, maintenance, preventive maintenance, remodeling, repair and servicing of the University's electrical systems from 12 volt up to and including 12,470 volts. Assembles, installs and repairs circuitry, switchgear, distribution systems and all related components. Frequently responsible for the training and supervision of less skilled workers. Work performed in an educational and research environment. This position will be located at our Dallas location: 2126 W Mockingbird Ln Dallas, TX 75235.</div> Facilities Management https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32497 2026-08-14T10:20:41-05:00 2026-08-14T10:20:42-05:00 Research Clinician <div>The Clinician role is responsible for delivering brain health assessments, coaching, and training services through the Center for BrainHealth. This role administers and interprets the Concierge BrainHealth Index, prepares reports, provides client feedback, and maintains ongoing client relationships. The position collaborates with an interdisciplinary team to develop individualized performance recommendations and support clinical research initiatives.<br><br></div><div>Responsibilities also include coaching research participants, scoring assessments, conducting virtual feedback sessions, facilitating group coaching, and managing participant communications through an online platform. The Clinician supports the planning and delivery of brain health training programs, develops training materials, and assists with recruitment and program evaluation.<br><br></div><div>In addition, the role provides administrative support including scheduling, client communications, and record maintenance. Success requires strong interpersonal, organizational, and communication skills; the ability to work independently and collaboratively; and a commitment to continuous improvement, participant experience, and compliance with HIPAA and IRB requirements. This position serves as a key member of the adult clinical research team while collaborating across the organization.</div> BrainHealth Project https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32267 2026-07-06T14:47:41-05:00 2026-07-06T14:47:42-05:00 Part-time Lecturer - Communication Studies <div>Lecturers teach one or more undergraduate and/or graduate sections in a given term. Appointments carry no guarantee or expectation of renewal or tenure.</div> Arts, Humanities, and Technology https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/31693 2026-04-14T12:31:53-05:00 2026-04-14T12:31:54-05:00 Research Associate <div>The Research Associate training program is designed as a 2-3 year experience that includes interdisciplinary team meetings, lab presentations, attendance at talks and medical Grand Rounds, journal article discussions, and training in cognitive and neuroimaging research. The fellow will gain experience in mentorship and grant-writing to transition the fellow into an independent scientist.<br><br></div> CBH Filbey https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32458 2026-08-07T07:39:04-05:00 2026-08-07T07:39:04-05:00 Vice President for Enrollment Strategy <div><strong>Position Overview</strong><br><br>The University of Texas at Dallas seeks an accomplished, visionary, and analytically sophisticated leader to serve as its next Vice President for Enrollment Strategy (VPES). Reporting directly to the Executive Vice President for Academic Affairs and Provost, the Vice President serves as the University's chief architect of enrollment strategy, responsible for aligning enrollment decisions with the University's academic aspirations, research trajectory, student success goals, institutional reputation, and long-term financial sustainability.<br><br>At one of the nation's fastest-rising public research universities, enrollment strategy is more than an operational function—it is a strategic imperative. As one of the University's principal strategic leaders, the Vice President will help shape institutional strategy by bringing deep expertise regarding enrollment markets, demographic trends, workforce needs, academic capacity, and the evolving higher education landscape. Working collaboratively across Academic Affairs, Student Affairs, Finance, Strategic Initiatives, Institutional Intelligence, University Communications, Global Engagement, and the academic schools, the Vice President will lead a comprehensive Strategic Enrollment Management enterprise that intentionally shapes the size, composition, quality, and success of the University's student body while advancing academic excellence, research distinction, innovation, and public impact.<br><br>The Vice President provides executive leadership for Undergraduate Admissions and Enrollment Management, the Office of the Registrar, and Financial Aid while cultivating a culture of innovation, collaboration, transparency, evidence-informed decision making, continuous improvement, and institutional stewardship.<br><br><strong>Leadership Competencies</strong></div><div>The Vice President for Enrollment Strategy will be a strategic and visionary leader who inspires innovation while building collaborative partnerships across the institution. The successful candidate will demonstrate exceptional analytical and data-informed decision-making, a steadfast commitment to academic excellence and student success, and the ability to lead complex initiatives with integrity, sound judgment, and responsible stewardship. This executive will serve as a trusted advisor to senior leadership, fostering a culture of collaboration, accountability, and continuous improvement.</div><div><strong><br>Note to Applicants:</strong> Please review the special instructions outlined below and ensure all requirements are met prior to submitting your application.<br><br><br></div> Academic Affairs and Provost Dept https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/30381 2025-09-24T17:06:43-05:00 2025-09-24T17:06:43-05:00 Maintenance Worker II <div><strong>Job Summary:</strong><br> Responsible for performing a variety of maintenance and repair tasks across one or more skilled trade areas, including carpentry, painting, flooring, drywall, and general maintenance.<br><br></div><div><strong>Please note:</strong> There are two vacancies available for this position.</div> Housing Operations https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32433 2026-07-31T17:15:24-05:00 2026-07-31T17:15:25-05:00 Program Manager - JSOM Abroad <div>The Program Manager supports the planning, coordination, and administration of programs and initiatives within JSOM Abroad. This role focuses on project management, logistics, contracts, budgeting, and general program support to ensure smooth and efficient operations. The Program Manager collaborates with faculty, staff, students, and campus partners to advance program goals and enhance the overall student experience.</div> Management https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32235 2026-07-01T16:52:43-05:00 2026-07-01T16:52:44-05:00 Part-Time Lecturer in Computer Science <div>Lecturers teach one or more undergraduate and/or graduate sections in a given term. Appointments carry no guarantee or expectation of renewal or tenure.</div> Computer Science https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32405 2026-07-28T08:32:25-05:00 2026-07-28T08:32:25-05:00 Police Officer <div>The University of Texas at Dallas Police Department is a component member of the UT System, dedicated to protecting and serving a dynamic university community. Our officers play a vital role in creating a safe and welcoming environment where teaching, research, and campus life can thrive.<br><br>At UT Dallas, policing goes beyond traditional law enforcement, it’s about building meaningful partnerships with students, faculty, staff, and visitors while fostering a culture of trust, respect, and integrity. Our officers work collaboratively across campus to prevent crime, respond to emergencies, and support a vibrant, growing academic community.<br><br><strong>Job summary</strong><br>To enforce the law; provide service, information and aid to all citizens as circumstances require; prevent crime; suppress disturbances; investigate criminal offenses; and arrest offenders. Responsible for enforcement duties for the protection, safety and welfare of students, employees, visitors, and all property within the area under the control and jurisdiction of The University of Texas System, including primary jurisdiction in all counties where the UT System has a real property interest and secondary jurisdiction in all other Texas counties. Exercises independent judgment within the limits prescribed by law, Rules and Regulations of the Board of Regents, institutional rules and regulations and Director of Police departmental policies and procedures. Other job duties as assigned.</div> University Police https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32200 2026-06-26T14:56:17-05:00 2026-06-26T14:56:17-05:00 Research Assistant I <div><br>We are recruiting a research assistant to support the Jiang Lab in the Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry at the University of Texas at Dallas. The research in the Jiang Lab focuses on the design of novel macromolecules (such as proteins/antibodies) to explore their biomedical applications.</div> Chemistry https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32565 2026-08-31T17:50:00-05:00 2026-08-31T17:50:01-05:00 Program Manager, Davidson Management Honors Program (JSOM) <div>The <strong>Program Manager</strong> serves as a key member of the <strong>Davidson Management Honors Program (DMHP)</strong> and is responsible for the planning, coordination, implementation, and assessment of programs and services that support student success, leadership development, engagement, recruitment, and community building. Reporting to the DMHP Director and working closely with the DMHP Associate Dean, this position plays an integral role in enhancing the undergraduate experience for approximately 2<strong>50 high-achieving business honors students</strong>.<br><br></div><div>The<strong> Program Manager </strong>serves as a primary point of contact for current and prospective students and collaborates with faculty, staff, alumni, and university partners to support a vibrant and engaged honors community. Responsibilities include student advising, leadership and mentoring programs, recruitment and admissions processes, student engagement initiatives, communications and marketing efforts, event planning, and program operations.<br><br></div><div>The successful candidate will be passionate about student development and committed to creating meaningful experiences that foster connection, belonging, academic excellence, and professional growth. This position requires significant interaction with students, occasional travel, and evening and weekend commitments to support recruitment activities, student events, conferences, competitions, retreats, and experiential learning opportunities.</div> Management https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32138 2026-06-17T17:04:07-05:00 2026-06-17T17:04:08-05:00 Police Telecommunicator <div>The primary function of a Police Telecommunicator is to receive and prioritize Emergency 9-1-1 and nonemergency telephone calls from the public. Enters information into a Computer-Aided Dispatch (CAD) system and processes non-emergency and routine requests for police and security services. Dispatch appropriate emergency services such as police, fire, and emergency medical services. Monitors public safety units in the field. Retrieves computer data for emergency response personnel within the service area. The Police Telecommunicator may provide alarm and closed-circuit television monitoring services while performing multiple tasks concurrently in a fast-paced environment, maintaining a professional and positive demeanor. Serves as a Campus Security Authority as defined by the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act).</div> University Police https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32555 2026-08-28T13:19:17-05:00 2026-08-28T13:19:17-05:00 Food Service Worker II <div>The <strong>Food Service Worker II</strong> at the Callier Child Development Center plays a vital role in supporting daily kitchen operations by assisting with food preparation, maintaining accurate records, and upholding high standards of quality and safety.<br><br>This position offers opportunities for growth through cross‑training in all areas of food service. The ideal candidate delivers excellent customer service, thrives in a team‑oriented environment, and can confidently read and follow recipes to ensure consistent, nutritious meal production.<br><br></div> Callier Ctr Communication https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32390 2026-07-23T13:36:02-05:00 2026-07-23T13:36:02-05:00 Coordinator of Spirit Programs <div>The Coordinator of Spirit Programs provides leadership for the University's spirit programs by overseeing the daily operations, strategic development, and continued growth of assigned spirit teams. This position cultivates a positive student experience while promoting school spirit, supporting campus traditions, representing the university at campus, community, and competitive events, and advancing the visibility and reputation of Comet Spirit Programs.</div> Student Development https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32036 2026-06-04T08:59:24-05:00 2026-06-04T08:59:25-05:00 Student Financial Aid Officer IV <div><strong>Are you interested in applying your experience and skills to help students achieve their educational goals? Are you looking for a rewarding and challenging opportunity in higher education that provides a hybrid work schedule and a comprehensive benefits package including employee tuition benefits?<br><br>The Office of Financial Aid is seeking a professional with experience in student aid or other higher education student and customer support to fill our Student Financial Aid Officer IV position. Apply now to join our team!</strong><br><br>The Student Financial Aid Officer IV will supervise the Financial Aid Customer Service Team, consisting of Student Financial Aid Officers and student workers who serve as the first point of contact for students and families in the Office of Financial Aid. The position will focus on providing excellent customer service in conjunction with the Financial Aid Counseling Team, and will also be responsible for performing a variety of duties associated with the coordination, awarding, and disbursement of federal, state, and institutional financial aid programs.</div> Office of Financial Aid https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32526 2026-08-25T08:15:15-05:00 2026-08-25T08:15:15-05:00 Finance Operations Coordinator <div><strong>Looking for a rewarding career opportunity with great benefits? Interested in joining a dynamic &amp; fun group of professionals? Look no further! Join our team!</strong><br><br> The University of Texas at Dallas has an excellent job opportunity for individuals looking to join the Erik Jonsson School of Engineering and Computer Science as a Finance Operations Coordinator.<br><br> This position will provide budgeting, finance, and procurement support for the Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering. The candidate will work closely with department faculty and staff to provide financial and research administration support for department finances, financial processes, and records to meet the department’s day-to-day financial goals. Additionally, this role will assist in ensuring that compliance with all regulations, policies and university requirements are met to secure the department’s long-term financial viability and stability</div> Electrical and Computer Engineering https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32375 2026-07-22T11:07:18-05:00 2026-07-22T11:07:18-05:00 Software Specialist I - JSOM <div><strong>*****YOUR NEXT OPPORTUNITY IS HERE***** APPLY TODAY!<br>Looking for a rewarding career opportunity with great benefits? Interested in joining a dynamic &amp; fun group of professionals? Look no further! Join our team!<br></strong><br></div><div>The University of Texas at Dallas has an excellent job opportunity for individuals looking to join our team as a Software Specialist I in the Jindal School of Management (JSOM).</div><div><br>Prepares new desktops and laptops for deployment by applying the standard JSOM image to them as they are received. Assist staff and faculty with data migration from old devices. Troubleshoot wireless network connectivity problems on Windows and Apple laptops and tablets as well as, Android and IOS devices. Additional duties as assigned.</div> Management https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32324 2026-07-13T18:17:14-05:00 2026-07-13T18:17:14-05:00 Research Administrator <div>The <strong>Research Administrator</strong> provides comprehensive pre-award and post-award support for research portfolios within the <strong>School of Behavioral and Brain Sciences (BBS)</strong>. This newly established position was created to formalize and strengthen research administration through a Grant Core model that embeds dedicated research support directly within academic departments.<br><br></div><div>Under this model, each department is supported by a full-time Research Administrator who reports directly to the Department Head and maintains a dotted-line relationship with the Sr. Director of Finance and Administration. This transition from a centrally managed structure to a department-based approach enables more specialized, responsive, and strategic support tailored to the unique needs of each department’s research portfolio.<br><br></div><div>The Research Administrator ensures compliance with University policies, sponsor guidelines, and federal regulations, including OMB 2 CFR 200 (Uniform Guidance), while providing support throughout the full lifecycle of sponsored projects—from proposal development and submission through award management and closeout. Through coordinated training, compliance oversight, quality assurance, and process improvement, the position advances the School’s research mission by promoting consistency, operational excellence, and high-quality service across all departments.</div> Neuroscience https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/31984 2026-05-27T11:22:42-05:00 2026-05-27T11:22:43-05:00 HVAC Technician <div>Performs preventative maintenance on HVAC equipment, this includes changing air filters, greasing, replacement of belts, etc. Installs motors, electronics, thermostats, humidistats, fans, other HVAC components, heating water and hydronics, chilled water controls and automated control systems. Assists with troubleshooting and resolving issues with HVAC equipment. Maintain a flexible work schedule including being on-call. Other duties as assigned. Must be willing to work weekends.</div> Facilities Management https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32503 2026-08-17T10:38:43-05:00 2026-08-17T10:38:43-05:00 Media Technology Specialist III <div>This position serves as the lead technician for the university's immersive projection classroom and is responsible for the preparation, setup, operation, maintenance, troubleshooting, and continued advancement of its Pixera-based visualization environment and associated audiovisual systems.<br><br>The position will diagnose and resolve complex technical issues, perform preventative maintenance, and ensure the reliable operation of the immersive classroom while serving as the technical lead for courses utilizing the immersive projection system. Working closely with faculty and staff, this position will provide technical guidance, production support, and training while collaborating on the design, development, and implementation of instructional content that maximizes the classroom's immersive technologies.<br><br>Under direct to general supervision provide faculty, staff and students with technical assistance, support, and policy and procedure orientation on media equipment capabilities and operations.</div> Educational Technology Services https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32269 2026-07-06T15:28:26-05:00 2026-07-06T15:28:26-05:00 Part-time Lecturer - Languages and Literature <div>Lecturers teach one or more undergraduate and/or graduate sections in a given term. Appointments carry no guarantee or expectation of renewal or tenure.</div> Arts, Humanities, and Technology https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/31853 2026-05-06T14:31:26-05:00 2026-05-06T14:31:26-05:00 Postdoctoral Research Associate <div><br>Postdoctoral positions (2) in the areas of peptide chemistry/engineering, protein engineering/design, and biocatalysis are available in the laboratory of Rudi Fasan in the Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry at the University of Texas at Dallas. Dr. Fasan is seeking candidates who are interested to work at the interface of chemistry and biology within a highly interactive and motivated group of colleagues. We are looking for enthusiastic and ambitious scientists with an established background in each of the relevant areas noted below. The candidates are expected to conduct research in one of the following areas:<br><br><strong>Area A:</strong><br><em>Research Focus</em> - synthesis and evolution of macrocyclic peptides as selective inhibitors/modulators of cancer-related targets.<br><em>Projects</em> - involve peptide chemistry, peptide engineering, and molecular display/selection technologies, and activity screening assays.<br><em>Established Background</em> - Organic/Bioorganic/Peptide Chemistry <br><br><strong>Area B: </strong><br><em>Research Focus</em> - design and development of engineered and artificial enzymes for biocatalysis and asymmetric synthesis<br><em>Projects</em> - involve biocatalysis, protein engineering/directed evolution/design, and mechanistic enzymology. <br><em>Established Background </em>- Biocatalysis/Protein Engineering/Enzymology <br><br><strong>Area C: </strong><br><em>Research Focus</em> - development and investigation of novel biocatalytic methods for asymmetric synthesis and selective functionalization of drug molecules.<br><em>Projects</em> - will involve organic synthesis, method development, biocatalysis and chemoenzymatic synthesis.<br><em>Established Background</em> - Organic Chemistry/Synthetic Methodology</div> Chemistry https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32464 2026-08-07T16:27:20-05:00 2026-08-07T16:27:20-05:00 Administrative Coordinator <div>The Administrative Coordinator provides high-level, complex, and confidential administrative support to the Director of Sleep and Innovation Laboratories at the Center for BrainHealth, University of Texas at Dallas. This position plays a central role in enabling the efficient execution of the director’s academic, research, administrative, public outreach, and strategic responsibilities. The Administrative Coordinator manages a high-volume and frequently shifting portfolio of activities, including executive scheduling, travel logistics, communications, meeting preparation, event coordination, financial and procurement support, technical and social media management, and liaison functions with internal and external stakeholders. The role requires sound judgment, discretion, exceptional organizational ability, and the capacity to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced academic and research environment. This position serves as a key coordination point across university leadership, faculty, staff, students, external collaborators, donors, media partners, and other professional constituencies.</div> CBH-Walker https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/31135 2026-01-16T00:02:49-06:00 2026-01-16T00:02:50-06:00 Postdoctoral Research Associate <div><br>The Sterling Group at the University of Texas at Dallas is seeking a postdoctoral researcher to explore polymer upcycling. Our research program integrates automated computational modelling, theoretical physical organic chemistry and electronic structure theory to advance our understanding of chemical reactivity. We aim to develop new concepts and computational tools to drive innovation across chemistry, biochemistry, materials science, and pharmaceutical research. We work closely with experimentalists to investigate reaction mechanisms, with an emphasis on catalysis and polymer chemistry.<br><br></div><div><br></div> Chemistry https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32445 2026-08-05T09:14:44-05:00 2026-08-05T09:14:44-05:00 Program Coordinator - Center for Global Business (JSOM) <div>The <strong>Program Coordinator</strong> plays a pivotal role in supporting the day-to-day coordination and execution of events, projects, and activities across the Center for Global Business (CGB)'s three core initiatives: the <strong>Global Talent &amp; Mobility Initiative (GTMI)</strong>, <strong>Global Development Initiative (GDI)</strong>, and <strong>Future Leaders Initiative (FLI)</strong> within the Jindal School of Management (JSOM) at The University of Texas at Dallas. This highly visible position also leads the coordination of recruitment, promotion, and program delivery for the <strong>Future Leaders Program (FLP)</strong>, helping to create impactful leadership development experiences for students.<br><br></div><div>The role is responsible for coordinating financial reconciliation, processing receipts and invoices, and maintaining accurate financial records and documentation. Working closely with CGB leadership, the CGB Student Council, the Jindal School community, and corporate partners, the Program Coordinator helps ensure programs and events are delivered efficiently, key milestones are met, and stakeholders remain engaged, informed, and connected to CGB's mission.<br><br></div><div>This is an outstanding opportunity for a highly organized, detail-oriented professional who thrives in a dynamic, collaborative environment and enjoys managing multiple priorities simultaneously. The ideal candidate is passionate about building relationships with students, alumni, industry leaders, and corporate partners, and is energized by the opportunity to contribute to high-impact initiatives that advance student success while bringing innovative, high-visibility programs and events to life.</div> Management https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32260 2026-07-06T10:57:33-05:00 2026-07-06T10:57:34-05:00 Building Automation System Specialist <div>Oversees the daily maintenance, operation, and repair of the campus building automation system. Monitors and troubleshoots system alarms. Inspect and improves the efficiency in equipment. Inspects work performed by contractors and provides staff training. Assigns work schedules to utilities station operators. Coordinates utilities operations with Energy Plant. Coordinates with other department for campus shut downs. Reviews mechanical system drawings and specifications. Assists EMS Supervisor with annual maintenance contracts and warranties. Maintains a flexible work schedule including being on-call.</div> Facilities Management https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32420 2026-07-30T09:24:39-05:00 2026-07-30T09:24:40-05:00 Lab Technician/Research Assistant <div>The <a href=\"http://labs.utdallas.edu/braincircuits\"><strong>Brain Circuits Laboratory</strong></a>, led by Drs. Steven Small and Ana Solodkin, is seeking a highly motivated Lab Technician with a strong interest in brain aging, neurodegeneration, and computational neuroscience. The position emphasizes research on macro-scale and multi-scale dynamic connectivity.<br><br></div><div>The successful candidate will also be responsible for supporting the administrative aspects of research studies, including scheduling, record-keeping, and coordination with human subjects. Proficiency with the Unix operating system is required, along with the ability to use brain imaging and network analysis software tools and to code in Python, R, and/or MATLAB.<br><br>Strong problem-solving abilities, sound judgment, and excellent interpersonal skills are essential for effectively troubleshooting, planning equipment and resource utilization, and interacting with lab members as well as older adult research participants.<br><br></div><div>The laboratory is located in the joint <a href=\"https://labs.utdallas.edu/braincircuits/contact/\"><strong>UT Dallas / UT Southwestern Texas Instruments Biomedical Engineering and Sciences Building (TI-BMES)</strong></a> on the campus of UT Southwestern. Address: 2336 Inwood Rd, Dallas, TX 75235</div><div><br></div><div><strong><em>The continued employment is contingent upon the availability of funds.</em></strong></div> Neuroscience https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32229 2026-07-01T14:44:26-05:00 2026-07-01T14:44:27-05:00 Part-Time Lecturer - Neuroscience <div>The School of Behavioral and Brain Sciences is seeking part-time lecturers with strong academic, clinical, or industrial neuroscience experience to teach undergraduate or graduate courses. Applicants with previous experience teaching should have a demonstrated record of teaching excellence.</div><div><br>This position will teach one or more undergraduate and/or graduate sections in a given term. Appointments carry no guarantee or expectation of renewal or tenure.</div><div>Applicants should upload a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy/experience (though not required), teaching evaluations (if available), and the full contact information for at least three academic or professional references; five (5) for those with no teaching experience.</div><div><br>Questions regarding this position can be sent to BBS.PeopleOps@utdallas.edu</div> Neuroscience https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32597 2026-09-02T11:17:15-05:00 2026-09-02T11:17:16-05:00 Network Engineer I <div>The Network Engineer I is an entry-level professional position responsible for supporting the operation, maintenance, and monitoring of the University of Texas at Dallas enterprise network infrastructure. This role works under the guidance of senior network engineers and management to ensure reliable, secure, and high-performing wired and wireless network services that support the academic, research, and administrative missions of the university.<br><br>This position emphasizes technical skill development, mentorship, and progressive responsibility within a collaborative environment.</div> Information Technology-Enterprise Tech. Innovation & Serv https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32147 2026-06-18T18:17:19-05:00 2026-06-18T18:17:20-05:00 Maintenance Worker III <div>Provide skills in the area of plumbing, electrical maintenance/repair, carpentry and/or painting.</div> Housing Operations https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32559 2026-08-28T16:28:36-05:00 2026-08-28T16:28:36-05:00 Postdoctoral Research Associate <div>The Department of Neuroscience and the Center for Advanced Pain Studies at UT Dallas has an opening for a postdoctoral research associate to join the Price Lab.<br><br></div><div>This specific position will work on NIH grant funded projects that are aimed at better understanding how neuronal plasticity alters the way the brain receives nociceptive information from the sensory system and how this relates to chronic pain. The project focuses on RNA sequencing, proteomic, and multiomic methods to understand the molecular make-up of human dorsal root ganglion cells and human spinal cord cells.<br><br><strong><em>This is a grant funded position, and continued employment is contingent on the availability of funds and satisfactory performance.</em></strong></div> Neuroscience https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32395 2026-07-23T17:26:16-05:00 2026-07-23T17:26:17-05:00 Child Development Assistant -  Infant/Toddler & Two's Program <div><strong>Looking for a rewarding opportunity to work with children? Join our Callier Center Team!<br><br></strong>The Callier Center provides a nurturing learning environment for infants through kindergarten age. We focus on developing every child’s specific needs, including communication and language skills, physical abilities, emotional and social growth, and cognitive development.<br><br>Our Program fosters an environment in which children have the opportunity to communicate, play and develop friendships with other children whose interests, abilities, levels of hearing, and methods of communication may be different than their own.<br><br>This position will assist in the provision of developmental program activities for infants and toddlers.</div> Callier Ctr Communication"
    },
    "https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/search.atom?query=&query_v0_posted_at_date=&query_position_type_id%5B%5D=2&commit=Search": {
      "title": "The University Of Texas At Dallas: All Jobs",
      "description": "tag:jobs.utdallas.edu,2005:/postings/search The University Of Texas At Dallas: All Jobs 2026-08-28T13:44:55-05:00 https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32558 2026-08-28T13:44:55-05:00 2026-08-28T13:44:55-05:00 Open-Rank Non-Tenure System Faculty position - Clinical Professor/Professor of Practice and Program Director <div><strong>Position Description</strong></div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>The Naveen Jindal School of Management is seeking a non-tenure track Clinical Professor/Professor of Practice and Program Director to lead the Alliance for Physician Leadership (APL) program, a nationally recognized Healthcare Leadership &amp; Management Executive MS/MBA exclusively for physician leaders.&nbsp; The program’s over 750 physician graduates currently occupy senior healthcare leadership roles throughout the United States.&nbsp; APL also offers healthcare certificate programs in partnership with healthcare systems for their emerging physician leaders. Appointment will be at the Assistant, Associate or full Professor rank, depending on experience.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>The Program Director’s role will be to collaborate with healthcare system leaders to assure program alignment with industry needs. The role collaborates on recruitment and selection of physicians and preservation of the program’s strong, supportive culture. The incumbent will also be expected to play an active role in program design and teaching; assuring program quality and financial success; coaching and mentoring aspiring physician leaders; recruiting and retaining appropriate faculty; and managing program staff. Extensive experience in healthcare leadership and operations and familiarity with current physician leadership issues are essential for this role.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>The successful candidate will be responsible for teaching graduate classes in Healthcare Administration. Curriculum oversight and ensuring that AACSB, university and school requirements are achieved, contributing assessment information and data as requested with an emphasis in sustainable practices.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>The preferred starting date is November 2026, teaching duties commence for the spring 2027 semester.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong>Qualifications</strong></div><div><strong>&nbsp;</strong></div><div>Minimum Education and Experience: A MS or equivalent in Healthcare Administration, Medical Management or a related discipline is required prior to employment. Candidates are expected to demonstrate the ability to work effectively in a highly collaborative, engaging, and dynamic environment comprised of individuals with a range of backgrounds, skills, and perspectives. We are seeking candidates able to deliver high quality teaching using evidence-based practices to effectively engage students from a range of backgrounds and experiences.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Preferred Education and Experience: PhD, MD or DO in Healthcare Administration, Medical Management or a related field. Substantial industry experience (at least five to ten years) in healthcare administration and familiarity with current physician leadership issues is strongly preferred and will weigh heavily in the review process.</div><div><strong>&nbsp;</strong></div><div><strong>The Department</strong></div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>The UT Dallas Executive Education area focuses on the education of working professionals through specialized corporate programs or certificate and degree options including Executive MBA and Executive MS options. &nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Degree emphasis and certificate topics include global marketing, healthcare, leadership, organizational consulting, project management, strategy, strategic human resources, supply chain. Corporate programs are typically customized to meet the needs of the client. &nbsp;</div><div><strong>&nbsp;</strong></div><div><strong>The Naveen Jindal School of Management</strong></div><div><strong>&nbsp;</strong></div><div>The Naveen Jindal School of Management has become a national and international leader in research and education since its own entrepreneurial beginning in 1975. Over 10,000 undergraduate and graduate students are enrolled in the Jindal School, the largest and fastest growing school at UT Dallas. With over 30 programs, we boast a diverse faculty and student body that provide an inclusive fusion of cultures and experiences.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong>Application Instructions</strong></div><div><strong>&nbsp;</strong></div><div>Applicants should upload the following:<a href=\"https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32549\"><strong> </strong></a><strong>&nbsp;</strong></div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>·&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Full curriculum vitae and cover letter summarizing their interests and qualifications for the position.</div><div>·&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Statement of teaching philosophy describing their conceptualizations of teaching and learning, and teaching and assessment methods, and how their teaching practices will engage students from a range of backgrounds and experiences.</div><div>·&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Full contact information for at least three academic or professional references.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Priority will be given to completed applications received by September 14, 2026. Reviews will continue until the position is filled or the search is closed on September 30, 2026.</div><div><strong>&nbsp;</strong></div><div><strong>The University and Community&nbsp;<br></strong><br></div><div>UT Dallas is a top public research university located in one of the nation’s fastest-growing metropolitan regions. Our seven schools offer 160 undergraduate and graduate degree programs, plus undergraduate and graduate certificates. Our student body is around 30,000 strong, reflecting students from over 100 countries and a multiplicity of perspectives and experiences. Over 60% of our undergraduate students receive some form of need- or merit-based financial aid, and 62% of graduating seniors have no student debt compared to 49% in all Texas publics and 51% in all national publics (<a href=\"https://www.utdallas.edu/about-us/fast-facts/\"><strong>UT Dallas Fast Facts</strong></a>).&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>Under the dynamic leadership of President Prabhas V. Moghe, UT Dallas is charting a path built on three strategic pillars – student success, academic and research convergence, and external impact. Guided by the <a href=\"https://roadmap.utdallas.edu/\"><strong>Roadmap 2030</strong></a> plan, UT Dallas will accelerate its upward trajectory to become a university of even greater impact and distinction.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>UT Dallas is committed to graduating well-rounded members of the community whose education has prepared them for rewarding lives and productive careers in a constantly changing world. Our mission centers on providing Texas and the nation with excellent and innovative education and research. The University’s rapid growth is fueled by our creative and enterprising spirt, bright students, innovative programs, renowned faculty, dedicated staff, engaged alumni, and research that matters.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>The University promotes a welcoming environment through programs and initiatives designed to support engagement and success for members of the campus community. Employee benefits include a range of physical and mental wellness resources, competitive insurance and retirement plan options, lactation facilities located throughout the campus, and Employee Resource Groups (ERGs) comprised of individuals who share common interests to help build community among UT Dallas faculty and staff (e.g., Universal Access ERG, Military and Veteran ERG, UT Dallas Young Professionals). Additionally, the University’s modern campus, 400+ campus organizations, and prime location foster collaboration and community.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Situated in Richardson, Texas, the University’s location offers abundant professional development and entertainment options. The Dallas-Fort Worth (DFW) metroplex is rich with visual and performing arts venues, museum districts, professional and semi-professional athletics teams, botanical gardens, accessible trails, and much more, ensuring there’s something for everyone. The University’s partnerships with regional higher education institutions, local school districts, numerous companies, and the Richardson Innovation Quarter (Richardson IQ) – a major hub for innovation, entrepreneurship, and educational activities – promotes collaboration, professional growth, and educational excellence.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong>Equal Employment Opportunity<br></strong><br> The University of Texas at Dallas is committed to providing an educational, living and working environment that is welcoming, respectful, and inclusive of all members of the university community. The University <a href=\"https://policy.utdallas.edu/utdbp3090\"><strong>prohibits unlawful discrimination</strong></a> against a person because of their race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, or veteran status.</div> Executive Education https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32530 2026-08-26T09:52:40-05:00 2026-08-26T09:52:40-05:00 Part-time Lecturer - Mechanical Engineering <div>Lecturers teach one or more undergraduate and/or graduate sections in a given term. Appointments carry no guarantee or expectation of renewal or tenure.</div> Mechanical Engineering https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32453 2026-08-06T08:23:09-05:00 2026-08-06T08:23:10-05:00 Part-Time Lecturer I & II (INTERNAL posting) <div>This internal posting is only to be used by internal applicants.<br><br>Lecturers teach one or more undergraduate and/or graduate sections in a given term. Appointments carry no guarantee or expectation of renewal or tenure.</div> Management https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32386 2026-07-23T09:55:42-05:00 2026-07-23T09:55:43-05:00 Part-time Lecturer - Criminology <div>Lecturers teach one or more undergraduate and/or graduate sections in a given term. Appointments carry no guarantee or expectation of renewal or tenure.</div> Criminology https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32384 2026-07-23T09:32:59-05:00 2026-07-23T09:32:59-05:00 Part-time Lecturer - Systems Engineering <div>Lecturers teach one or more undergraduate and/or graduate sections in a given term. Appointments carry no guarantee or expectation of renewal or tenure.</div> System Engineering https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32346 2026-07-16T10:52:17-05:00 2026-07-16T10:52:18-05:00 Part Time Lecturer - JSOM Capstone Senior Projects <div>Lecturers teach one or more undergraduate and/or graduate sections in a given term. Appointments carry no guarantee or expectation of renewal or tenure.</div> Management https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32270 2026-07-06T15:50:50-05:00 2026-07-06T15:50:51-05:00 Part-time Lecturer - Visual and Performing Arts <div>Lecturers teach one or more undergraduate and/or graduate sections in a given term. Appointments carry no guarantee or expectation of renewal or tenure.</div> Arts, Humanities, and Technology https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32269 2026-07-06T15:28:26-05:00 2026-07-06T15:28:26-05:00 Part-time Lecturer - Languages and Literature <div>Lecturers teach one or more undergraduate and/or graduate sections in a given term. Appointments carry no guarantee or expectation of renewal or tenure.</div> Arts, Humanities, and Technology https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32268 2026-07-06T15:02:42-05:00 2026-07-06T15:02:42-05:00 Part-time Lecturer - History and Philosophy <div>Lecturers teach one or more undergraduate and/or graduate sections in a given term. Appointments carry no guarantee or expectation of renewal or tenure.</div> Arts, Humanities, and Technology https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32267 2026-07-06T14:47:41-05:00 2026-07-06T14:47:42-05:00 Part-time Lecturer - Communication Studies <div>Lecturers teach one or more undergraduate and/or graduate sections in a given term. Appointments carry no guarantee or expectation of renewal or tenure.</div> Arts, Humanities, and Technology https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32266 2026-07-06T14:36:22-05:00 2026-07-06T14:36:22-05:00 Part-time Lecturer - Media Arts and Design <div>Lecturers teach one or more undergraduate and/or graduate sections in a given term. Appointments carry no guarantee or expectation of renewal or tenure.</div> Arts, Humanities, and Technology https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32261 2026-07-06T11:58:54-05:00 2026-07-06T11:58:55-05:00 Part-time Lecturer - Animation and Games <div>Lecturers teach one or more undergraduate and/or graduate sections in a given term. Appointments carry no guarantee or expectation of renewal or tenure.</div> Arts, Humanities, and Technology https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32238 2026-07-02T08:49:46-05:00 2026-07-02T08:49:46-05:00 Part-time Lecturer - Electrical and Computer Engineering <div>Lecturers teach one or more undergraduate and/or graduate sections in a given term. Appointments carry no guarantee or expectation of renewal or tenure.</div> Electrical and Computer Engineering https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32235 2026-07-01T16:52:43-05:00 2026-07-01T16:52:44-05:00 Part-Time Lecturer in Computer Science <div>Lecturers teach one or more undergraduate and/or graduate sections in a given term. Appointments carry no guarantee or expectation of renewal or tenure.</div> Computer Science https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32231 2026-07-01T15:09:32-05:00 2026-07-01T15:09:32-05:00 Part-time Lecturer - Audiology or Speech/Language Pathology <div>The School of Behavioral and Brain Sciences is seeking part-time lecturers with expertise in speech-language pathology or audiology to teach undergraduate or graduate courses. Applicants with previous experience teaching should have a demonstrated record of teaching excellence.</div><div><br>This position will teach one or more undergraduate and/or graduate sections in a given term. Appointments carry no guarantee or expectation of renewal or tenure.<br><br></div><div>Applicants should upload a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy/experience (though not required), teaching evaluations (if available), and the full contact information for at least three academic or professional references; five (5) for those with no teaching experience.</div><div><br>Questions regarding this position can be sent to <a href=\"mailto:BBS.PeopleOps@utdallas.edu\"><strong>BBS.PeopleOps@utdallas.edu</strong></a></div> Speech Language Hearing https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32230 2026-07-01T14:57:35-05:00 2026-07-01T14:57:35-05:00 Part-time Lecturer - Psychology <div>The School of Behavioral and Brain Sciences is seeking part-time lecturers with expertise in Psychology to teach undergraduate or graduate courses. Applicants with previous experience teaching should have a demonstrated record of teaching excellence.</div><div><br>This position will teach one or more undergraduate and/or graduate sections in a given term. Appointments carry no guarantee or expectation of renewal or tenure.</div><div><br>Applicants should upload a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy/experience (though not required), teaching evaluations (if available), and the full contact information for at least three academic or professional references; five (5) for those with no teaching experience.</div><div><br>Questions regarding this position can be sent to <a href=\"mailto:BBS.PeopleOps@utdallas.edu\"><strong>BBS.PeopleOps@utdallas.edu</strong></a></div> Psychology https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32229 2026-07-01T14:44:26-05:00 2026-07-01T14:44:27-05:00 Part-Time Lecturer - Neuroscience <div>The School of Behavioral and Brain Sciences is seeking part-time lecturers with strong academic, clinical, or industrial neuroscience experience to teach undergraduate or graduate courses. Applicants with previous experience teaching should have a demonstrated record of teaching excellence.</div><div><br>This position will teach one or more undergraduate and/or graduate sections in a given term. Appointments carry no guarantee or expectation of renewal or tenure.</div><div>Applicants should upload a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy/experience (though not required), teaching evaluations (if available), and the full contact information for at least three academic or professional references; five (5) for those with no teaching experience.</div><div><br>Questions regarding this position can be sent to BBS.PeopleOps@utdallas.edu</div> Neuroscience https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/32142 2026-06-18T10:12:47-05:00 2026-06-18T10:12:47-05:00 Part-Time Lecturer - Mathematical Sciences <div>Lecturers teach one or more undergraduate and/or graduate sections in a given term. Appointments carry no guarantee or expectation of renewal or tenure.<br><br>Applicants should upload a curriculum vitae.<br><br></div> Mathematical Sciences https://jobs.utdallas.edu/postings/29871 2025-07-17T13:25:07-05:00 2025-07-17T13:25:08-05:00 Part-time Lecturer - Chemistry <div>Lecturers teach one or more undergraduate and/or graduate sections in a given term. Appointments carry no guarantee or expectation of renewal or tenure.</div> Chemistry"
